WEBVTT

00:20.846 --> 00:22.544
- Hi, baby.
- Hey.

00:22.631 --> 00:24.720
- Oh, your hair looks nice.
- Oh, thank you.

00:24.763 --> 00:26.504
Much better
than the last time I saw it.

00:26.504 --> 00:28.202
It was all ratty.

00:28.289 --> 00:29.986
Made me want
to stick a match to it.

00:30.073 --> 00:32.032
Uh-huh. You ready to go?
Y-You got everything?

00:32.075 --> 00:33.946
Just let me find my...

00:33.990 --> 00:35.731
Oh, no. I'll drive.
That's...

00:35.731 --> 00:38.168
- Uh-uh.
- You sure?

00:38.212 --> 00:40.475
- Morning, y'all.
- Hey. Good morning, Dad.

00:40.518 --> 00:42.520
- How's retirement treating you?
- Good.

00:42.520 --> 00:44.305
See y'all later.

00:45.784 --> 00:47.743
He's not coming with us?

00:47.786 --> 00:50.746
Uh-uh. He's busy.

00:50.746 --> 00:52.139
Your car is too little.

00:52.226 --> 00:54.228
Let's take mine.

00:57.970 --> 01:01.757
♪ Somebody prayed for me♪

01:01.800 --> 01:05.195
♪ Had me on their mind♪

01:05.195 --> 01:07.980
♪ They took that time
and prayed for me♪

01:08.024 --> 01:09.591
♪ Oh, yes, they did...♪

01:09.678 --> 01:11.984
Can we stop somewhere
and get something to eat?

01:11.984 --> 01:16.467
No time. Got to pick up Grandpa
and Jeanie.

01:16.554 --> 01:19.383
I thought you weren't talking
to Aunt Jeanie anymore.

01:19.470 --> 01:22.343
We started again.

01:22.386 --> 01:24.736
That's good.

01:24.823 --> 01:27.087
She's been keeping Dad.

01:27.130 --> 01:29.741
Grandpa?

01:29.785 --> 01:31.526
Yeah. I don't like it.

01:34.572 --> 01:36.705
Why not?

01:36.705 --> 01:39.186
She's a mess.

01:39.229 --> 01:41.797
She's a hoarder.
Old nasty house.

01:41.840 --> 01:43.799
She just wants Dad
living with her

01:43.842 --> 01:45.540
so she can collect his pension.

01:45.583 --> 01:47.977
She's lost her mind.

01:48.064 --> 01:48.978
♪ Hallelujah...♪

01:49.065 --> 01:50.414
I'm gonna steal him from her.

01:54.026 --> 01:56.899
What? You're gonna
steal him from her?

01:56.899 --> 02:00.859
Mm-hmm. Any time I try to see
him or say hi, she won't let me

02:00.946 --> 02:03.775
unless she's there to supervise.
She has lost her mind.

02:03.819 --> 02:06.517
Lost her damn mind.

02:26.189 --> 02:30.237
Right. That's what I told him.

02:30.280 --> 02:33.240
Mm-hmm. If you want them
to adjust your vacation days,

02:33.283 --> 02:37.287
you got to talk to Nancy in HR.

02:37.331 --> 02:39.420
That's the way I used to do it.

02:39.420 --> 02:40.856
Yeah.

02:40.899 --> 02:42.640
Morning.

02:42.684 --> 02:44.860
No, man.

02:44.860 --> 02:47.863
I'm trying to get like you.

02:47.863 --> 02:50.344
Hey, look,
I'm-a have to let you go.

02:52.302 --> 02:54.304
Yeah, I'm here
to get that new phone.

02:54.304 --> 02:56.567
You know the one
with the night vision?

02:56.567 --> 02:58.874
Yeah.

02:58.874 --> 03:01.137
All right. Take it light.

03:01.224 --> 03:02.834
I'll catch up with you later.

03:05.141 --> 03:07.099
-♪ God is♪
-♪ God is♪

03:07.099 --> 03:09.537
♪ Oh♪
♪ My everything...♪

03:09.537 --> 03:12.235
Can we, um, stop
to get some food real fast?

03:12.279 --> 03:14.977
We'll be late.

03:15.020 --> 03:17.371
Dig in my purse and get you some
cough drops if you're hungry.

03:19.938 --> 03:21.940
I'm okay, thank you.

03:22.027 --> 03:23.507
Thank you, Auntie.

03:26.031 --> 03:27.816
How's your baby, Earn?

03:29.948 --> 03:32.299
Oh, she's good. She's good.

03:32.342 --> 03:34.344
She's, um...
she's not really a baby anymore.

03:34.344 --> 03:36.041
- That's the thing...
- You didn't want
to bring her to church?

03:38.261 --> 03:40.045
She's, uh...
she's with her mom today.

03:40.045 --> 03:43.353
Mm. Hey.

03:43.353 --> 03:45.355
Y'all still ain't married, huh?

03:45.355 --> 03:47.096
You know
they not married, Jeanie.

03:47.183 --> 03:49.533
Hmm.

03:49.577 --> 03:51.927
Well, it's a good thing
you coming to church then, Earn.

03:51.927 --> 03:54.669
You can ask for forgiveness.

03:54.712 --> 03:56.758
Mm-hmm.

03:56.845 --> 03:59.543
For laying
with that beautiful girl

03:59.630 --> 04:01.545
and leaving her in sin.

04:01.632 --> 04:02.546
Aah!

04:02.633 --> 04:04.766
Get the fuck off the road!

04:04.853 --> 04:06.942
Jesus.

04:06.942 --> 04:09.336
♪ Yes, sir, yes, sir,
come on, God is...♪

04:20.303 --> 04:22.087
Let me get Daddy over here.

04:25.656 --> 04:27.658
Ooh. You help me, Earn?

04:53.423 --> 04:54.729
-♪ No matter what♪
-♪ No matter what♪

04:54.772 --> 04:57.645
♪ You happen to go
through right now♪

04:57.688 --> 04:59.951
♪ Remember that
in the midst of it♪

04:59.995 --> 05:04.869
♪ God only wants to use you♪

05:04.869 --> 05:07.002
-♪ No matter what it is♪
-♪ No matter what♪

05:07.002 --> 05:09.265
♪ That you're going through♪

05:09.352 --> 05:10.788
♪ Hold your head up...♪

05:10.788 --> 05:12.529
You know, it's packed in here.

05:12.573 --> 05:14.836
She probably had to go
to the overflow lot.

05:14.923 --> 05:18.013
Why would she need
to go to the overflow lot?

05:18.013 --> 05:20.363
She has Daddy's handicap pass.

05:20.407 --> 05:23.148
She should be parked by now.

05:23.192 --> 05:25.455
Yeah... um...

05:25.499 --> 05:27.196
You check your phone?
She call you back?

05:28.980 --> 05:31.243
No.

05:31.243 --> 05:33.158
It's your mama.

05:33.158 --> 05:34.943
- It's your mama.
- Yeah.

05:34.943 --> 05:36.553
Yes, it is.

05:36.597 --> 05:39.164
- Yeah, she's a trip.
- Mm-hmm.

05:39.164 --> 05:41.602
She's a real trip. Um...

05:44.648 --> 05:45.997
I got to use the bathroom.

05:46.041 --> 05:47.608
Yeah. This don't make no sense.

05:47.608 --> 05:49.218
Yeah.

05:49.261 --> 05:51.351
Don't make no kind of sense.

05:59.750 --> 06:01.622
Hello?

06:01.622 --> 06:03.275
Hey, Dad.

06:03.319 --> 06:05.060
Hey, what's going on, son?

06:05.103 --> 06:07.671
Yeah, um,
I'm with Mom, and, um,

06:07.758 --> 06:10.892
I think she kind of took Granda

06:10.935 --> 06:12.241
and left me holding the bag
with Aunt Jeanie.

06:12.328 --> 06:14.548
Mm-hmm.

06:14.635 --> 06:15.679
I'm trying to know
how you would handle this.

06:15.766 --> 06:18.639
Really can't answer that.

06:18.682 --> 06:20.467
Taking my day.

06:20.554 --> 06:22.730
I get three hours every Sunday

06:22.730 --> 06:26.473
before the kids show up
at the mall. This is my time.

06:26.560 --> 06:29.301
- It's like that? 
- It's like that.

06:29.301 --> 06:31.260
I've been dealing
with this family

06:31.303 --> 06:34.611
for 30 years.
You'll be okay for one day.

06:34.655 --> 06:36.396
I'm sure
you'll do the right thing.

06:36.439 --> 06:38.267
Love you.

06:38.310 --> 06:39.921
Yeah.

06:52.542 --> 06:55.066
John chapter ten,
verse ten says,

06:55.110 --> 06:57.417
"The thief does not come
except to steal

06:57.460 --> 06:59.288
and to kill and to destroy."

07:03.901 --> 07:05.642
I guess you and your mama
must think

07:05.686 --> 07:08.428
I'm stupid, Earn.

07:08.471 --> 07:09.864
What?

07:12.475 --> 07:15.609
I wasn't born yesterday, now.

07:15.696 --> 07:17.872
I watch Criminal Minds,
and I know

07:17.915 --> 07:20.396
when someone's up
to something twisted.

07:20.483 --> 07:23.138
What-what are you talking about?

07:23.138 --> 07:26.750
Your mama stole Daddy,
and you helped her do it.

07:26.837 --> 07:28.535
- No.
- Where did she take him?

07:28.622 --> 07:31.146
- I don't know.
- Earnest.

07:31.146 --> 07:34.497
I don't know, Aunt Jeanie.
I don't know.

07:38.370 --> 07:40.895
What you sneaking
out of church for, then? Hmm?

07:40.938 --> 07:42.984
Where you going?

07:43.071 --> 07:45.334
I'm going to the studio.

07:45.377 --> 07:47.075
I'm supposed
to meet Alfred there. I'm late.

07:47.075 --> 07:49.730
You know, so...

07:50.992 --> 07:53.951
So?

07:53.995 --> 07:56.867
- So?
- So...

08:00.523 --> 08:02.743
So?

08:05.223 --> 08:07.704
So I guess
I'm going to the studio, too.

08:07.748 --> 08:09.924
You're not leaving my sight.

08:12.970 --> 08:15.582
Come on here now.

08:43.479 --> 08:45.525
Sorry, I'm on a schedule.

08:47.657 --> 08:49.659
- Excuse me, sir...
- No. Sorry.

08:49.659 --> 08:50.704
- Not interested.
- Has anyone told you,

08:50.791 --> 08:53.010
you would look really great
in a hat?

08:53.010 --> 08:56.361
Uh... no.

08:56.361 --> 08:58.668
I'm serious.

08:58.712 --> 09:00.670
Not everyone can pull off a hat,
you know,

09:00.670 --> 09:02.716
but you have
a very nice-shaped head.

09:04.021 --> 09:05.936
Well...

09:05.936 --> 09:07.851
I...

09:07.938 --> 09:10.158
- Thank you for that.
- Hey,

09:10.245 --> 09:14.728
I am not going to make you buy
anything, unless you want to.

09:14.815 --> 09:17.339
You seem too strong-willed
for that kind of thing, anyway.

09:19.820 --> 09:21.648
- Brah!
- Yellow.

09:21.735 --> 09:23.998
Again?

09:24.041 --> 09:26.217
- Man, the color yellow, man.
- You cheating.

09:26.261 --> 09:28.219
Nigga, how you cheat
at Uno, man? Hey, y'all...

09:28.263 --> 09:30.091
Y'all ever cheat at Uno?
Anybody know? How you cheat?

09:30.178 --> 09:31.832
You know I don't got
no more yellow cards.

09:31.875 --> 09:33.703
Duh, nigga!
That's the point of the game!

09:33.747 --> 09:35.487
That's how the game is played,
man. That's how you play that.

09:35.487 --> 09:37.011
So, see,
I was trying to be polite,

09:37.054 --> 09:39.274
but now I want you to draw four.
Fuck that.

09:39.274 --> 09:42.277
Eight, nigga,
'cause you out here whining.

09:42.320 --> 09:43.931
I ain't playing
with you no more.

09:43.974 --> 09:46.063
Oh, come on, man, you know I...

09:50.067 --> 09:51.765
- Hey, y'all hear that shit?
-♪ Now they call me Mr. Ruffle♪

09:51.852 --> 09:53.505
♪ 'Cause I'm all
about my chips...♪

09:53.505 --> 09:57.684
...all day until you tell me
where my daddy is, okay?

09:57.727 --> 09:59.207
You think it's gonna be
fun time in the studio?

09:59.207 --> 10:01.078
I don't think so.

10:01.078 --> 10:01.992
Aunt Jeanie?

10:01.992 --> 10:03.385
Out.

10:03.428 --> 10:05.300
Everybody out.

10:05.300 --> 10:07.258
This is a family emergency.

10:07.345 --> 10:09.521
Yeah, come on...

10:09.565 --> 10:12.263
- Let's go, let's go...
- Go on, now, get on!

10:12.307 --> 10:13.656
I'm-a call you, bro.
I'm sorry, man.

10:13.656 --> 10:16.050
Go!

10:17.660 --> 10:19.401
Thank you.

10:19.444 --> 10:21.490
I like your earrings, baby.

10:21.577 --> 10:22.926
Thank you, ma'am.

10:23.013 --> 10:24.885
Mm-hmm.

10:27.757 --> 10:29.498
Hey, look, now, this ain't
got nothing to do with me.

10:29.541 --> 10:31.369
All right? So I don't know
nothing about Aunt Gloria

10:31.456 --> 10:33.328
taking Grandpa, stashing him.
I don't know that.

10:33.328 --> 10:36.070
So you in on this, too, huh?

10:36.113 --> 10:37.462
- She ain't know that?
- No.

10:37.462 --> 10:40.291
Ain't that a "B"?

10:40.335 --> 10:43.164
This whole family is against me.

10:43.251 --> 10:45.557
- Yeah.
- I'll be...

10:45.601 --> 10:47.342
Where'd she take him?

10:47.385 --> 10:50.519
- Why don't you call her? Damn.
- I don't know.

10:50.562 --> 10:53.653
Okay. I-I know what I'm-a do.
I know what I'm-a do.

10:53.696 --> 10:56.264
I'm-a fix y'all. Y'all watch.

11:01.486 --> 11:03.271
- Hello.
- Willy.

11:03.271 --> 11:04.707
Willy, it's Jean.

11:04.751 --> 11:06.535
I need you to add Pearl.

11:06.622 --> 11:08.537
All right.

11:08.624 --> 11:09.886
Hello.

11:09.930 --> 11:11.235
Pearl.

11:11.279 --> 11:12.497
It's Jeanie.

11:12.541 --> 11:15.196
I need you to add Gloria.

11:18.373 --> 11:19.374
What?

11:19.374 --> 11:21.332
Y'all, y'all.

11:21.419 --> 11:24.379
Gloria kidnapped Dad.

11:24.379 --> 11:26.816
Oh, my goodness.

11:26.816 --> 11:27.991
Girl, have you lost your mind?

11:28.078 --> 11:29.384
Look,

11:29.384 --> 11:31.038
you can't kidnap your own dad.

11:31.038 --> 11:32.692
I don't have time to explain it
to you right now,

11:32.735 --> 11:34.432
but the word "kid" is in it.

11:34.519 --> 11:36.521
So, mathematically,
it's impossible.

11:36.565 --> 11:38.610
What? No, she took him!

11:38.654 --> 11:40.395
She sped off with him.

11:40.395 --> 11:42.397
He is confused, and he needs me.

11:42.440 --> 11:45.095
Y'all know he has dementia.

11:45.182 --> 11:48.403
And I'm the only one who knows
how to give him his medicine.

11:48.403 --> 11:49.404
Jeanie,

11:49.404 --> 11:50.361
that man ain't got dementia.

11:50.448 --> 11:51.798
He's just old, just old.

11:51.885 --> 11:54.452
He forgot something
one or two times.

11:54.496 --> 11:57.412
Why don't you just tell her
how to give him his medicine?

11:57.412 --> 11:59.849
I mean, really,
how complicated could it be?

11:59.893 --> 12:02.765
I knew
I couldn't count on y'all.

12:02.765 --> 12:05.202
I knew it.
I mean, this one thing.

12:05.246 --> 12:07.901
And y'all didn't help me pay
for Keisha's college.

12:07.988 --> 12:10.294
- We did, too, help.
All of us did. 
- And you didn't help me

12:10.294 --> 12:13.645
sue that crooked mailman,
and you ain't helping me now.

12:13.645 --> 12:15.778
Y'all are bitter towards me.

12:15.822 --> 12:18.128
And don't think
I don't know why.

12:19.695 --> 12:21.610
Why?

12:21.697 --> 12:23.786
Y'all have always hated me.

12:26.223 --> 12:29.226
Ever since we were kids. Because...

12:32.664 --> 12:35.624
Y'all hate me
because I'm light-skinned.

12:43.937 --> 12:47.549
Girl, if you don't get the hell
out of here with all that mess.

12:47.549 --> 12:50.508
Nobody hates you 'cause you're
light-skinned, Your Majesty.

12:50.595 --> 12:52.684
Girl, I hate you
because you're evil.

12:52.684 --> 12:54.469
I bet you won't be complaining

12:54.469 --> 12:56.471
about being light-skinned-ed
if the cops came down there.

12:56.514 --> 12:58.690
What? Oh, I should
call the cops?

12:58.734 --> 13:00.823
- I wish you would.
- Please do.

13:00.823 --> 13:04.218
Uh, do not call the cops, please.

13:04.261 --> 13:06.220
Y'all...

13:06.263 --> 13:09.005
I know exactly
what this is really about.

13:11.268 --> 13:14.054
WILLY [sighs]:
What? What is it about?

13:14.054 --> 13:17.231
It's about Daddy
never remembering Gloria.

13:17.274 --> 13:20.495
I mean, Daddy got kids
all over Georgia,

13:20.538 --> 13:22.627
and he can remember
most of them,

13:22.627 --> 13:25.108
but never little Gloria.

13:25.195 --> 13:27.850
I mean, he didn't remember
her birthday, Christmas,

13:27.894 --> 13:30.287
didn't come to graduation.

13:30.331 --> 13:33.551
And now that he's dying,
you can't even talk to him

13:33.638 --> 13:36.337
because he don't know
who you are.

13:36.380 --> 13:38.208
I bet you haven't even
asked him, have you, Gloria?

13:48.088 --> 13:50.046
That was evil.

13:50.090 --> 13:51.439
You evil.

13:55.312 --> 13:57.097
While I still
got you on the phone,

13:57.097 --> 13:59.447
you do remember
that you owe me $800

13:59.447 --> 14:00.665
for student...

14:09.544 --> 14:12.199
- Yeah.
- I think it definitely might be

14:12.242 --> 14:14.114
my favorite one
that you tried so far.

14:14.157 --> 14:16.072
- You think?
- Mm-hmm.

14:16.116 --> 14:18.118
I mean, it does look
like something I could

14:18.118 --> 14:20.163
wear to play cards
with the guys.

14:20.250 --> 14:22.078
Right, right, right.

14:22.122 --> 14:24.298
Do you want to try
on the number three again?

14:24.341 --> 14:25.603
Yeah.

14:33.263 --> 14:34.961
Does anything
even look bad on you?

14:36.963 --> 14:38.616
You know...

14:38.703 --> 14:40.488
Never mind.

14:40.488 --> 14:42.359
What?

14:42.359 --> 14:44.361
No, you know...

14:44.361 --> 14:46.146
No, come on, tell me.

14:51.499 --> 14:53.762
I have this one hat.

14:53.805 --> 14:56.156
It's not on display,

14:56.156 --> 14:58.985
because it's technically,
it's not for sale yet.

14:59.072 --> 15:02.597
But you are
so handsome and nice,

15:02.640 --> 15:04.773
I think I want
to show it to you.

15:04.816 --> 15:07.428
Okay. Uh, but I don't want to
get you in trouble or anything.

15:07.515 --> 15:08.995
Ah! Trouble.

15:13.521 --> 15:14.826
♪ Love...♪

15:14.826 --> 15:18.004
A special person deserves

15:18.091 --> 15:20.397
a special hat.

15:20.397 --> 15:22.791
Wow.

15:22.834 --> 15:25.576
-♪ Love.♪
- Hmm.

15:27.100 --> 15:28.579
Does your sister have any
history with weapons or drugs?

15:28.666 --> 15:30.625
She might.

15:30.625 --> 15:33.889
She don't. She don't.

15:34.759 --> 15:37.197
Officer... my father

15:37.240 --> 15:40.026
is scared and alone,
and he is confused.

15:40.113 --> 15:42.158
I guarantee you he doesn't even

15:42.202 --> 15:43.594
recognize Gloria.

15:43.681 --> 15:45.379
That's how sick he is.

15:45.422 --> 15:47.555
Okay, hold on.

15:49.687 --> 15:51.994
Can we get your mom
on the phone?

15:51.994 --> 15:54.127
Yeah. Yeah.

16:13.668 --> 16:14.669
Hello.

16:14.669 --> 16:17.324
Hi, Mom. It's Earn.

16:17.324 --> 16:19.500
Um, the cops are here
with Aunt Jeanie.

16:19.587 --> 16:21.067
They need to check on Grandpa.

16:23.243 --> 16:25.506
Hey, can you put
your father on, please?

16:34.384 --> 16:36.430
Hello.

16:36.473 --> 16:38.040
Hello, sir.
We're doing a wellness check.

16:38.040 --> 16:39.607
Is everything okay?

16:39.607 --> 16:41.435
Yeah.

16:41.478 --> 16:43.654
Do you know where you are, sir?

16:43.741 --> 16:46.440
Of course I do.

16:46.483 --> 16:48.790
Are you in any danger?

16:48.833 --> 16:51.097
No.

16:51.184 --> 16:53.316
Ain't no danger here.

16:55.623 --> 16:57.320
Ask him do he know
who he's with.

16:57.364 --> 16:59.279
And do you know
who you're with, sir?

16:59.322 --> 17:01.498
He won't know.

17:01.498 --> 17:03.500
I'm with my daughter.

17:03.500 --> 17:04.849
Gloria.

17:07.069 --> 17:08.549
So, you're not in any danger.

17:08.636 --> 17:10.029
You know where you are
and who you're with, sir?

17:10.072 --> 17:12.770
Yeah.

17:12.857 --> 17:15.338
We're in Egypt.

17:15.425 --> 17:17.340
Been here...

17:17.427 --> 17:19.777
two weeks.

17:19.864 --> 17:21.562
Okay.

17:21.649 --> 17:23.520
Thank you, Officer...

17:23.520 --> 17:25.261
You see that?

17:25.305 --> 17:27.916
Did-did-did you see that?
I told you.

17:28.003 --> 17:30.136
They in Egypt.

17:40.537 --> 17:44.324
♪ There's something
that I want to give you...♪

17:44.367 --> 17:47.022
Hey!

17:47.109 --> 17:50.330
♪ A five-pound box of love♪

17:50.330 --> 17:52.767
♪ With a million-dollar bill
on top♪

17:52.767 --> 17:54.812
♪ Million-dollar bill on top♪

17:54.899 --> 17:57.119
♪ Diamonds on every corner...♪

18:10.915 --> 18:13.570
Oh, my God.

18:13.570 --> 18:15.355
Church is out.

18:28.933 --> 18:32.807
Yo, Pops.
Yo, Pops.

18:32.807 --> 18:35.549
Hold on, man,
let me ask you a question.

18:37.812 --> 18:39.770
What's on your head, Pops?

18:39.857 --> 18:42.425
It's my hat.

18:42.469 --> 18:45.080
And what's wrong
with your hat?

18:45.167 --> 18:48.475
Y'all know what this nigga
remind me of?

18:48.518 --> 18:50.825
You look like--
what's that nigga name, Prince?

18:50.825 --> 18:52.783
This nigga look like Prince.

18:52.827 --> 18:54.742
If Prince never died
and became some old, fat nigga.

18:57.875 --> 18:59.399
Yo, I got to get a picture
of this stupid-ass hat.

18:59.399 --> 19:00.661
I don't think so.

19:00.748 --> 19:02.271
Hey, hey, come...
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa,

19:02.271 --> 19:04.055
come on, I'm just playing
with you, homie.

19:04.099 --> 19:07.058
Got to get a picture for the,
you know, Gram, like...

19:07.058 --> 19:08.843
Look, I'm late.
I ain't got time for this.

19:08.843 --> 19:11.062
Whoa, come...

19:11.106 --> 19:12.847
Late? What you mean, you late?

19:12.847 --> 19:15.415
You ain't gonna take a picture?
So, I got to beg?

19:15.458 --> 19:17.895
Pops? That's what you want?

19:19.767 --> 19:21.986
I'll do it.

19:24.337 --> 19:25.555
I'm-a beg, Pops.

19:28.254 --> 19:30.604
Begging now, Pops.

19:33.563 --> 19:35.217
On my knees, Pops.

19:35.261 --> 19:37.828
I'm on my knees.

19:37.872 --> 19:39.874
It's what you wanted, ain't it?

19:39.917 --> 19:41.745
Just get up.

19:41.789 --> 19:44.574
As long as I get a picture, I'll
get up, that's all I'm saying.

19:44.661 --> 19:46.489
I'm staying right here.
I'm-I'm cool right here.

19:46.533 --> 19:48.274
- Get up. I'll-I'll take
the picture. Just get up.
- Please?

19:48.361 --> 19:50.798
Oh, you'll take the picture?
Oh, shit.

19:50.885 --> 19:52.452
That's all you had to say, then,
Pops. That's all I wanted...

19:55.455 --> 19:57.196
Man.

20:04.028 --> 20:06.727
Shit about to go viral, Pop.

20:06.814 --> 20:09.077
I like the hat, Pops.

20:13.168 --> 20:14.648
- Excuse me?
- Do you know what...?

20:14.691 --> 20:16.127
She is really not
gonna let us leave, is she?

20:16.127 --> 20:18.217
You normally do wellness checks
over the phone?

20:22.569 --> 20:24.527
You could've took her anywhere,
Earn. Anywhere.

20:24.614 --> 20:26.181
Yeah, and she would've
followed me there.

20:26.268 --> 20:27.748
I was gonna come to you
eventually, relax.

20:30.054 --> 20:32.187
Damn.

20:32.274 --> 20:34.450
Man, I'm just giving you
a hard time, man.

20:34.494 --> 20:36.931
I know. I just...

20:36.974 --> 20:39.716
I just don't want to end up
like them.

20:39.716 --> 20:41.718
What you mean?

20:41.762 --> 20:43.503
Arguing all the time.

20:51.989 --> 20:54.905
Hey.

20:54.949 --> 20:57.908
Hey, yo, uh, miss. Um...

20:57.952 --> 21:00.911
Look, y'all got a-- y'all got
another way out of here?

21:00.998 --> 21:03.914
Like a secret way?

21:06.526 --> 21:08.484
There's another way out back.

21:08.528 --> 21:10.704
Word?

21:10.747 --> 21:13.141
We call it the Shmurda exit.

21:13.184 --> 21:15.796
Bobby had it built when he was
recording here for a month.

21:15.883 --> 21:19.539
He had the FBI
and three baby mamas after him.

21:19.539 --> 21:20.757
Couldn't take any chances.

21:20.757 --> 21:22.759
Didn't help him, though.

21:22.759 --> 21:24.935
- Mm-mm.
- No.

21:24.979 --> 21:27.547
But it might help you.

21:35.859 --> 21:38.775
Yes, I would like
to report a kidnapping.

21:38.775 --> 21:41.169
No, I know
that the cops are here,

21:41.212 --> 21:42.823
but they are not doing
their job, okay?

21:42.910 --> 21:45.565
Wait, nah, nah,
th-this ain't gonna work.

21:45.608 --> 21:47.262
She's gonna see us.

21:47.349 --> 21:50.221
Don't worry, she won't see you.

21:50.265 --> 21:54.617
The only thing is, you can't
look back, not even a glance.

21:54.704 --> 21:56.750
That's how this works.

21:56.793 --> 21:58.621
Can you be here within the hour?

22:00.014 --> 22:01.929
I also need you to arrest

22:01.929 --> 22:04.410
my two nephews.

22:04.453 --> 22:07.804
No, Officer Simone
and-and French,

22:07.848 --> 22:09.980
they're not doing their job.

22:10.024 --> 22:12.505
No, sir.
No, it's-it's a kidnapping.

22:14.507 --> 22:17.510
No, I'm-I'm-- I-I would like
to report a kidnapping, okay?

22:19.294 --> 22:21.122
:
My father has been kidnapped
by my sister.

22:24.386 --> 22:26.475
I know he's not a kid.

22:26.475 --> 22:28.303
Okay, you know, can I speak
to your manager, please?

23:14.218 --> 23:15.394
Mmm. That was good.

23:15.437 --> 23:17.265
Good dinner.

23:17.308 --> 23:18.614
That was not dinner.

23:18.658 --> 23:20.660
Well, what was it, then?

23:20.703 --> 23:21.878
I don't know.

23:21.922 --> 23:23.184
But it's 5:00 p.m.

23:23.227 --> 23:24.707
It's not dinner.

23:27.710 --> 23:29.886
Hey, Pops, you okay?

23:29.930 --> 23:31.584
How was the mall?
You get that phone?

23:31.671 --> 23:34.151
I got it.
It's-it's good.

23:34.238 --> 23:35.675
I hope you didn't
get anything else.

23:35.718 --> 23:37.938
- I didn't.
- Good.

23:38.025 --> 23:40.244
'Cause our Mastercard
last month was too high.

23:40.288 --> 23:43.422
More sweet tea for you, ma'am?

23:43.465 --> 23:44.945
- Oh, I, um...
- No, just the bill.

23:45.032 --> 23:46.250
Yeah, and I can get it.

23:46.250 --> 23:48.035
No, no, I got it, I got it.

23:50.472 --> 23:52.256
- Oh, shoot!
- What?

23:52.300 --> 23:53.693
We didn't get any bread.

23:53.693 --> 23:55.738
Um, excuse me.

23:55.825 --> 23:57.523
Mom, dinner's already over.

23:57.610 --> 23:58.959
We-we don't need the bread.

23:59.046 --> 24:00.700
I mean, we're paying
real money for the food

24:00.743 --> 24:02.310
like everybody else.

24:02.353 --> 24:04.181
We deserve to get bread

24:04.268 --> 24:05.705
like everybody else.

24:05.705 --> 24:07.881
And besides, your grandfather
loves that bread.

24:07.924 --> 24:09.317
- Yes, ma'am?
- Oh, we didn't get any bread.

24:09.404 --> 24:10.971
Oh, I'm sorry about that.

24:11.058 --> 24:13.974
Can you maybe bring us some?

24:14.017 --> 24:15.715
Uh, sure. Do you want me
to hang on to the bill?

24:15.715 --> 24:17.630
No, you can bring the bill

24:17.717 --> 24:19.719
and just put the bread
in a to-go box.

24:19.762 --> 24:22.461
Um, let me go check real fast.

24:22.504 --> 24:23.723
"Go check"?

24:23.723 --> 24:26.377
We don't normally
pack bread to go.

24:26.377 --> 24:28.336
You never brought us
any bread in the first place,

24:28.379 --> 24:29.772
so I don't see
how that could be a problem.

24:29.859 --> 24:32.601
There's no problem.
I just got to go ask my boss.

24:32.645 --> 24:34.908
Oh, honey, we could pack
that bread ourselves.

24:34.951 --> 24:36.170
Yeah, but I just got to ask...

24:36.213 --> 24:39.216
Just bring the goddamn bread!

24:44.526 --> 24:46.572
Bring us the bread.

24:48.312 --> 24:50.010
Right. Okay.

24:50.097 --> 24:51.490
Right away, sir. Sorry.

24:54.014 --> 24:55.972
Kids.

24:56.016 --> 24:58.279
Just don't have any respect.

24:58.322 --> 25:00.107
No respect at all.

25:15.209 --> 25:17.777
Y'all want to watch
a Redbox tonight?

25:19.126 --> 25:20.736
Yeah.

25:22.433 --> 25:25.349
♪ We've got to do something,
yeah♪

25:25.393 --> 25:27.961
♪ To save the children♪

25:34.576 --> 25:37.797
♪ Soon it will be their turns♪

25:37.840 --> 25:40.843
♪ To try and save the world♪

25:46.806 --> 25:51.071
♪ Right now they seem to play♪

25:51.158 --> 25:54.509
♪ Such a small part of♪

25:59.688 --> 26:03.997
♪ The things that they'll soon♪

26:04.040 --> 26:08.088
♪ Be right at the heart of♪

26:12.179 --> 26:14.834
♪ My little Tommy♪

26:14.834 --> 26:19.578
♪ He said he wants
to be a fireman.♪

26:25.409 --> 26:26.106
Captioned by
Media Access Group at WGBH
